  "node --input-type=module -e 'import assert from \"node:assert/strict\"; import { createRequire } from \"node:module\"; const coverage = createRequire(import.meta.resolve(\"@vitest/coverage-v8\")); const parent = createRequire(coverage.resolve(\"magicast\")); const { SourceMapConsumer } = parent(\"source-map-js\"); assert.throws(() => new SourceMapConsumer({version: 3, sections: [{offset: {line: 10000001, column: 0}, map: {version: 3, sources: [\"a.js\"], names: [], mappings: \"AAAA\"}}]}), /must not exceed/u);'",project,120,"harness:codex","2026-10-06T00:34:41.703Z",local_mutation,fix/source-map-security-worker-debug-output,Independent known-advisory control using the actual development parent resolution. Constructor only; never serializes an oversized offset. Same control is a relevant safe failure on source-map-js1.2.1 and passes on1.2.2 even when advisory feeds lag.
